-- EXPECT-ERROR: expected `String` but got `Int`
-- Slice 6 (nested-module soundness), the ENTRY-MODULE variant -- the same
-- `id`-launder soundness break, but through the ENTRY module's own top-level
-- fn referenced by its SELF-QUALIFIED name `Main.id`. `check_module_core`
-- seeds the entry module's own unannotated top-level fns under a self-qualified
-- key (`Main.id`) while the nested-prefix accumulator (`cap_qual_prefix`) is
-- still empty, so the round-2 nested reconcile (gated `cap_qual_prefix <> ""`)
-- structurally excluded it; an explicit `Main.id(42)` reference kept a
-- decoupled scheme and erased `Int -> String` (exit 0 pre-fix). A BARE `id`
-- was always safe (desugar never auto-qualifies bare refs), but the written
-- `Main.id` form is memory-unsafe. The P0 fix (round 3) reconciles BOTH the
-- `cap_qual_prefix` key AND the `current_module` key, so `Main.id` is now the
-- real polymorphic `a -> a`. IMPOSSIBLE to reject pre-fix. See
-- core-march-types.md §2.8.13.
mod Main do
  fn id(x) do x end

  fn need_str(s : String) : Int do string_length(s) end

  fn attack() : Int do need_str(Main.id(42)) end
end
